[
  {
    "body": "Every endpoint below lives under `https://api.acme.dev/v2` and speaks JSON\nwith UTF-8 encoding.",
    "content_hash": "70536a8bb763c7381ea87b778e3bf23cd3b133af024ccee9fe68ee4b6c1da8e7",
    "header": "[acme 2.1.0 › Acme API Reference]",
    "page_range": [
      22,
      117
    ],
    "section_path": [
      "Acme API Reference"
    ],
    "token_count": 33
  },
  {
    "body": "The API accepts bearer tokens only. Send the key in the `Authorization`\nheader; a key scoped to a project sees that project's widgets and nothing\nelse.\n\n```http\nAuthorization: Bearer sk-test-not-a-real-key\n```",
    "content_hash": "8e8b9d02366bebebe93dde0937565155c7582852149b8d96e0e95e6db36a7031",
    "header": "[acme 2.1.0 › Acme API Reference › Authentication]",
    "page_range": [
      138,
      347
    ],
    "section_path": [
      "Acme API Reference",
      "Authentication"
    ],
    "token_count": 66
  },
  {
    "body": "Rotation issues a second key that runs beside the first for one week. Both\nkeys stay valid during the overlap, so a deploy can cut over without a\nmaintenance window.",
    "content_hash": "9d0a2473be950f348d6fb746871365b6d5183a16f3dc6b7280b2d0c9abfa7094",
    "header": "[acme 2.1.0 › Acme API Reference › Authentication › Key rotation]",
    "page_range": [
      367,
      532
    ],
    "section_path": [
      "Acme API Reference",
      "Authentication",
      "Key rotation"
    ],
    "token_count": 58
  },
  {
    "body": "`GET /widgets` returns the project's widgets ordered by creation time.\n\n```json\n{ \"widgets\": [{ \"id\": \"w_01\", \"kind\": \"plain\" }], \"nextCursor\": null }\n```",
    "content_hash": "53f97ad80004e9675a69aa176886eb3a0b6f7ec88a29dc1ba68df203f8e820d4",
    "header": "[acme 2.1.0 › Acme API Reference › Widgets › List widgets]",
    "page_range": [
      564,
      718
    ],
    "section_path": [
      "Acme API Reference",
      "Widgets",
      "List widgets"
    ],
    "token_count": 54
  },
  {
    "body": "`POST /widgets` accepts the `kind` field and returns the created row. A\nduplicate name inside one project answers `409` with the existing row in the\nbody.",
    "content_hash": "01592455f1224ac0ff8646d6952e9c248c3c09a4b5af5ddd25ec8af7e35e3b5a",
    "header": "[acme 2.1.0 › Acme API Reference › Widgets › Create a widget]",
    "page_range": [
      741,
      895
    ],
    "section_path": [
      "Acme API Reference",
      "Widgets",
      "Create a widget"
    ],
    "token_count": 55
  },
  {
